Perhaps this was an intentional change / correction - it caught me out because previously dataframes were acceptable.

R code to demonstrate:

library(rstan)
Y=data.frame(cbind(rnorm(20)),cbind(rnorm(20)))

sm='data{
  vector[2] Y[20];
}
parameters{
  real mu;
}
model{
  mu~normal(0,1);
for(i in 1:20){
  Y[i] ~ normal(mu,1);
}

}
'
stan(model_code=sm,data=list(Y=Y),iter=200)
stan(model_code=sm,data=list(Y=as.matrix(Y)),iter=200)

I'd recommend target += instead of increment_log_prob (which is deprecated), but if you do want to use increment_log_prob then it should work if you use "+" instead of "," between the terms.

Jonah

