You just need to call a user-defined function that returns the lower bound, like

functions {
  real lb(matrix X, vector beta) {
    real max_mu = max(exp(X * beta));
    if (max_mu <= 2) return max_mu / (max_mu - 4);
    return -1;
  }
}

Then, in the parameters block

parameters {
  vector[K] beta;
  real<lower=lb(X, beta), upper = 1> lambda;
}

Ben

