Sorry I missed this the first time around.

Usually you want to scale the correlation matrix into
a covariance matrix.  There's a discussion in the manual chapter
on regression.

Also, I'm not sure why you're giving the imputed values two
distributions, one with

>   imps ~ normal(0,2);

and one with:

>       for (n in 1:N) {
>         y_normal_i[n,v] = missingL[n,v] ? imps[missing_counter[n,v]] : y_normal[n,v];

> ...
>   y_normal_i ~ multi_normal_cholesky(i_mu, i_L_Omega);

You should probably just get rid of the first one (normal(0, 2)).

- Bob

